# Pavilion vs SHMS deploys

Build **Pavilion** demo/marketing as its own product surface. No Stone Hill PII or school cost on Pavilion.

Stone Hill (`frontend` / www.shmspto.org) and Pavilion apps share historical frontend code but are **separate products**:

- **shmspto** = canonical source + live school
- **pavilion** = consumer; catches up when Rob asks

## Stone Hill ships (~/shmspto workspace)

See **`shms-deploy-git.mdc`**. Summary:

1. Edit, Serena QA, commit in **`auraflux-dev/shmspto`**
2. Staging review on **https://shmspto.vercel.app** when visitor-facing (Rob OK)
3. **`git push origin main`** on **`shmspto`**
4. **`node scripts/check-prod-deploy.mjs`**

Staff-only: push `shmspto` `main` after Serena QA, then run the check script.

**Do not** sync or deploy Pavilion as a follow-up unless Rob asked.

## Pavilion ships (this workspace, opt-in)

- **Pavilion-only tasks:** commit + deploy `commons-site`, `commons-pto-demo`, `commons-pto` as relevant.
- **Demo catch-up from school:** Rob must ask → `--from-shms --apply` → commit pavilion → deploy demo (vanilla; no SHMS branding on Pavilion surfaces).

Never put Stone Hill Wix / Square env on Pavilion projects, or Pavilion Stripe on Stone Hill.

At session start: `node scripts/commons-parity.mjs` is informational. Do not force catch-up unless Rob wants Pavilion updated.

Plaid stays on the **Trial** account until paying Pavilion clients.

After a Pavilion-facing ship, run `node scripts/commons-surface-check.mjs`.
